5) Should you itemize or take the standard deduction?
- Standard deduction (2023, Married Filing Jointly): $27,700.
- Likely itemized deductions you listed: $1,400 charity (plus any state/local taxes you paid and mortgage interest if applicable). Because SALT is capped at $10,000 and you didn’t list big deductible items, it’s very likely the standard deduction is larger.
- Recommendation: take the standard deduction unless you have additional deductible items (large state/local taxes, mortgage interest, big medical expenses over 7.5% of AGI, large charitable donations, etc.) that you have not listed.

