- Copies of any 1099s (1099‑NEC, 1099‑INT, 1099‑DIV, 1099‑B) if you want me to estimate actual tax and self-employment tax liability.

9) Recommendations
- Likely take the standard deduction ($27,700) given the small charitable amount you listed — but confirm other deductible items (mortgage interest, property tax).
- Use actual-cost home office deduction (allocating rent/utilities) rather than the simplified method, since actual allocation of rent yields a higher deduction for your numbers.
- Claim student loan interest up to the $2,500 limit (unless your joint MAGI is high because of spouse income).
- Report self-employment income on Schedule C and SE; pay estimated taxes if you expect to owe more than safe harbor thresholds.
- Keep Form 1098‑E, 1099s, receipts for charity, and documentation for home office and business expenses.

