3. Do you want me to (a) produce a one‑page checklist to hand to your CPA, (b) estimate your tax liability more precisely if you give me exact additional expenses/withholdings, or (c) draft an email to your tax preparer with the numbers and documents needed?

Caveats
- I’m giving general guidance based on the facts you provided; tax law is complex and sometimes fact‑sensitive. For final filing, especially because you have self‑employment income, home‑office calculations, and the student-loan interest amount above the $2,500 limit, I recommend you either use a reputable tax software or consult a CPA/tax preparer to confirm exact numbers, ensure correct forms (esp. QBI interactions), and check for any state-specific differences.

If you want, tell me whether the $650 are business expenses and whether you want me to run a more precise estimate (include other expenses, tax withholdings, or any estimated payments you made). I can then update the calculations or draft a summary to send to an accountant.

