- Conclusion: It’s almost certainly better to take the standard deduction. Even if you itemized, the student loan interest deduction and the half SE tax deduction are above-the-line and available whether or not you itemize.

8) Forms you’ll likely need
- Form 1040 — main return.
- Schedule 1 (Additional Income and Adjustments) — for student loan interest deduction (and other adjustments).
