- Interest income = $2,100.
- Total income ≈ 82,350 + 6,025 + 2,100 = 90,475.
- SE tax on net self-employment (approx): ~ $852; half SE tax deductible ≈ $426.
- Student loan interest paid claimed up to $2,500 (max) — assume you qualify for full $2,500 for this example.
- Adjustments to income ≈ $2,500 (student loan) + $426 (half SE tax) = $2,926.
- Estimated AGI ≈ 90,475 − 2,926 = 87,549.
- Standard deduction 27,700 leaves taxable income ≈ 59,849.

